    "result_text": "The build is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. The audit log confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (REGION `NSW` + FY `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + Luhn CHK `1`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced the `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns with a single `member_id` column + `getMemberId()`/`setMemberId()`; removed the instance `getCheckDigit()` and replaced it with a reusable static `luhnCheckDigit(String)` that computes the CHK over `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`; rewired `getLocality()` and `getFiscalYear()` to read the REGION and FY segments off the `memberId` (a new private `memberIdRegion()` extracts the leading-letters region, which is cleanly delimited by the numeric FY).\n- **`AssignMemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 replaces `AssignCustomerCode` and `AssignMembershipNumber` (both deleted). Builds `REGION + FY + HASH8 + CHK`, with collision de-duplication now applied to the `memberId` (`-<n>` suffix). FY comes from the business-day-adjusted registration date set earlier in the pipeline.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 collapsed the two assign steps into one `assignMemberId` step.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java` / `OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 the audit line and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carry `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` schema properties with `memberId`, removed `checkDigit`, and updated the `fiscalYear`/`locality` descriptions to reference the `memberId` (these DTOs are code-generated from this schema and mapped by name via MapStruct).\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 replaced the two columns with a single `member_id`.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId`) and all existing tests pass.\n\nNote: I interpreted \"the fiscal-year value ... must reference the memberId\" as `getFiscalYear()` reading the FY segment out of the `memberId` (mirroring how `locality` reads the REGION segment), rather than recomputing from the registration date. The computed value is identical for created owners; if you'd prefer `getFiscalYear()` to keep deriving directly from the registration date, that's a one-line change.",
