        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe restructuring is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Two functions collapsed into one is the right unit.** `AssignCustomerCode` + `AssignMembershipNumber` were only separate because the membership number was derived from the customer code. With a single unified `memberId`, a single `AssignMemberId` function is the natural home, and it keeps the same shape (region derivation, E.164 normalization, `hash8`, collision de-dup loop) as the function it replaces \u2014 a maintainer would recognize it immediately.\n\n- **`getCheckDigit()` \u2192 `static luhnCheckDigit(String)` is a clean, well-motivated extraction.** The Luhn logic now needs to run at assignment time (to build the CHK segment) rather than per-response, so turning it into a reusable pure static that takes the value is correct placement. Keeping it on `Owner` as `public static` matches the existing idiom there (`fiscalYear`, `regionOfPostcode`, `postcodeRangeOf` are all static domain helpers on `Owner`), and `public` is justified since `AssignMemberId` lives in a different package.\n\n- **The new `memberIdRegion()` private helper avoids duplication.** Both `getLocality()` and `getFiscalYear()` need to locate the REGION prefix; factoring the leading-letters scan into one documented helper is better than repeating the parse, and it's appropriately scoped as private.\n\n- **No new catch-all.** `Owner` was already the accumulation point for derived getters and static identity helpers; this change swaps like-for-like rather than growing a grab-bag, and even nets a removed field (`checkDigit`) and getter.\n\n- **The dependent consumers are all updated consistently and in the right places** \u2014 audit line/event, OpenAPI schema, all four DB schemas, and the YAML step wiring \u2014 with docs rewritten to point at `memberId` rather than left stale. The stale forward-looking comment in `OwnerCreatedEvent` was correctly collapsed to the now-realized state.\n\nNothing is misplaced, duplicated, or becoming a catch-all."
